{"title":"Career Roadmap: Lab Analyst","role":"Lab Analyst","summary":"A Lab Analyst performs laboratory testing, sample analysis, documentation and quality-control activities across sectors such as:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Life Sciences / Biological Sciences"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build laboratory testing, analytical, biological, quality-control, data-analysis and documentation skills for laboratory and research environments"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Lab Analyst performs laboratory testing, sample analysis, documentation and quality-control activities across sectors such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Food and beverage"},{"text":"Environmental testing"},{"text":"Agriculture"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Consumer products"},{"text":"Industrial laboratories"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact responsibilities depend on the laboratory. A Life Sciences graduate can be well suited to biological and analytical laboratory roles, but specialized clinical, pharmaceutical or regulated testing positions may require additional qualifications."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof to Create","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"1st Year"},{"text":"Biology & chemistry foundation"},{"text":"Cell biology, biochemistry, chemistry"},{"text":"Laboratory practical portfolio"},{"text":"Weak scientific fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2nd Year"},{"text":"Laboratory techniques"},{"text":"Microbiology, molecular biology, analytical methods"},{"text":"Experimental reports"},{"text":"Limited hands-on practice"}],[{"text":"3rd Year"},{"text":"Analytical & quality skills"},{"text":"Instrumentation, statistics, QA/QC"},{"text":"Laboratory analys